#{[17592186476895 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476895 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109857" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476895 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476895 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following subspaces must be orthogonal to $\\text{Null}({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})$ for all compatible matrices $X$ and $Y?$\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(YX)$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})$\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(YX)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476895 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d68ce86-72b3-53d7-b424-c8c3717fc180" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476895 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that $\\text{Null}({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})$ contains all vectors that, when pre-multiplied by ${X}^{T}{Y}^{T},$ result in the zero-vector $0.$ \n\nWhen pre-multiplying a vector by ${X}^{T}{Y}^{T},$ we actually multiply each row of ${X}^{T}{Y}^{T}$ by that vector. So, $\\text{Null}({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})$ must be orthogonal to the row space of ${X}^{T}{Y}^{T},$ which is $\\text{Col}(({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})^{T})=\\text{Col}(YX).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de22dd5b352e1d5be48f4b6ed3b2a4657ae623c1bd288d3464559758ea334af7.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476920 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476920 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109863" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476920 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476920 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A$ and $B$ be $m\\times n$ matrices. What is the image of ${R}^{m}$ under the action of ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476920 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "814b73ba-57d5-52a9-8c36-0c9f156faa4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476920 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}$ is a $n\\times m$ matrix.\n\nNow, pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{m}$ by ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}$ gives a linear combination of the columns of ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n{{\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{1} & ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{2} & ⋯ & ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{m} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{T}+{B}^{T}}\\cdot {{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{m}\\end{bmatrix}}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{1} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{2} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}+⋯+{x}_{m}\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{m} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{m}$ under the action of ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}$ must be $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T}),$ the row space of $A+B.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186476953 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476953 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108924" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476953 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476953 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A$ be a $m\\times n$ matrix. What is the image of $\\text{Null}({A}^{T})$ under the action of ${A}^{T}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476953 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bb821d7a-e914-5964-b025-342c273fea77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476953 #edb/ref 1074 "By definition of the null subspace, $\\text{Null}({A}^{T})$ is mapped to the zero vector $0$ under the action of ${A}^{T}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186477097 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186477097 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186477097 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f20cbbab-e838-5cc3-9bc0-309fc77b0b95" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186477098 #edb/ref 1080 "true" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186477098 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186477098 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56ed48d0-e778-5305-b095-810cb0318a7c" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186477099 #edb/ref 1080 "false" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186477099 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [1759218647