d2dd-2260-5a76-91a1-48cb49a84605" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565990 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565990 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186565990 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c36cab80-11fb-53dd-8c1f-1830080636ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566092 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566092 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566092 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fb4475e7-9df7-5f01-8da5-2b4f45ddcbb7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566119 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566119 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565865 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566119 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566119 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186565990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566119 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186566092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566119 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566119 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566119 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186565871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566119 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "24c992c9-8052-5ffe-8e34-a8bb4e14e451" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566271 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186566119 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566271 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109851" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566271 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566271 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following subspaces must be orthogonal to $\\text{Null}(B)$ for every matrix $B?$\n\nI. $\\text{Null}({B}^{T})$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(B)$\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}({B}^{T})$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566271 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f11ffdfd-619b-56d9-be79-9ad5a11a6df9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186566271 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that $\\text{Null}(B)$ contains all vectors that, when pre-multiplied by $B,$ result in the zero-vector $0.$ \n\nWhen pre-multiplying a vector by $B,$ we actually multiply each row of $B$ by that vector. So, $\\text{Null}(B)$ must be orthogonal to the row space of $B,$ which is $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $B$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/18/18713ed3d103ca0a02d74cede1e6448012e0aa28a2df804d41cfb277589a0158.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
